<svg viewBox="0 0 900 402" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Traceability matrix with populated rows">
<!-- FIGURE 15.1 REQUIRED ELEMENTS
Must appear: a populated traceability matrix with at least three real
rows connecting a requirement identifier, requirement statement, control,
evidence, and status, including at least one row whose status is a
qualified "partially met" rather than a clean pass, demonstrating that the
evidence column can contradict what the control column alone would imply.
Entry condition: requirements have been written under 15.1. Exit
condition: each requirement's actual verification status is visible from
the evidence, not assumed from the existence of a control. Deliberately
excluded: model card structure (Figure 15.2's job). Must work in black
and white.
SOURCE: original; the matrix follows this chapter's own section 15.2
example, built from the FairLend and MedAssist running cases.
AUDIT: pass 1 [x] against list, pass 2 blind [ ], rendered and viewed [x]
-->
<title>Traceability matrix with populated rows</title>
<style>
text{font-family:'Source Sans Pro','Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;}
.ttl{font-size:17px;font-weight:700;}
.cls{font-size:14px;font-weight:700;}
.bx{font-size:12.5px;font-weight:400;}
.col{font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.06em;}
.sm{font-size:11px;font-weight:400;}
.em{font-size:11px;font-style:italic;}
</style>
<rect x="0" y="0" width="900" height="402" fill="#ffffff"/>
<text x="20" y="34" class="ttl" fill="#1a2230">Figure 15.1 &#183; Traceability matrix with populated rows</text>
<text x="30" y="62" class="col" fill="#46536b">ID</text>
<text x="90" y="62" class="col" fill="#46536b">REQUIREMENT</text>
<text x="380" y="62" class="col" fill="#46536b">CONTROL</text>
<text x="570" y="62" class="col" fill="#46536b">EVIDENCE</text>
<text x="770" y="62" class="col" fill="#46536b">STATUS</text>
<line x1="20" y1="76" x2="880" y2="76" stroke="#1a2230" stroke-width="1.6"/>
<rect x="20" y="90" width="860" height="72" rx="4" fill="#eef1f5" stroke="#1a2230" stroke-width="1.2"/>
<text x="32" y="112" class="bx" font-weight="700" fill="#1a2230">FL-014</text>
<text x="90" y="110" class="sm" fill="#46536b">Adverse action notice states</text>
<text x="90" y="126" class="sm" fill="#46536b">specific denial factors (ECOA)</text>
<text x="380" y="110" class="sm" fill="#46536b">Explanation module generates</text>
<text x="380" y="126" class="sm" fill="#46536b">factor-ranked output at denial</text>
<text x="570" y="110" class="sm" fill="#46536b">50-sample review of denial</text>
<text x="570" y="126" class="sm" fill="#46536b">explanations, Q2 2026</text>
<rect x="770" y="106" width="78" height="26" rx="3" fill="#1a2230"/>
<text x="809.0" y="123" class="sm" font-weight="700" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">MET</text>
<rect x="20" y="174" width="860" height="72" rx="4" fill="#eef1f5" stroke="#1a2230" stroke-width="1.2"/>
<text x="32" y="196" class="bx" font-weight="700" fill="#1a2230">FL-015</text>
<text x="90" y="194" class="sm" fill="#46536b">Explanation understandable to</text>
<text x="90" y="210" class="sm" fill="#46536b">a layperson, not just accurate</text>
<text x="380" y="194" class="sm" fill="#46536b">Explanation output reviewed</text>
<text x="380" y="210" class="sm" fill="#46536b">against plain-language standard</text>
<text x="570" y="194" class="sm" fill="#46536b">Readability scoring on same</text>
<text x="570" y="210" class="sm" fill="#46536b">50-sample set: 12 of 50 flagged</text>
<rect x="770" y="190" width="78" height="26" rx="3" fill="#8a3324"/>
<text x="809.0" y="207" class="sm" font-weight="700" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">PARTIAL</text>
<rect x="20" y="258" width="860" height="72" rx="4" fill="#eef1f5" stroke="#1a2230" stroke-width="1.2"/>
<text x="32" y="280" class="bx" font-weight="700" fill="#1a2230">MA-007</text>
<text x="90" y="278" class="sm" fill="#46536b">Sensitivity ≥ 0.85 for sepsis</text>
<text x="90" y="294" class="sm" fill="#46536b">onset, per site, quarterly</text>
<text x="380" y="278" class="sm" fill="#46536b">Quarterly retest per</text>
<text x="380" y="294" class="sm" fill="#46536b">hospital site</text>
<text x="570" y="278" class="sm" fill="#46536b">Q3 2026 retest: community</text>
<text x="570" y="294" class="sm" fill="#46536b">hospital site not yet rerun</text>
<rect x="770" y="274" width="78" height="26" rx="3" fill="#8a3324"/>
<text x="809.0" y="291" class="sm" font-weight="700" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">UNMET</text>
<line x1="20" y1="350" x2="880" y2="350" stroke="#c9d1dc" stroke-width="1"/>
<text x="20" y="368" class="sm" fill="#46536b">The evidence column, not the control column, decides status: FL-015 and MA-007 both have a control in place,</text>
<text x="20" y="386" class="sm" fill="#46536b">but the evidence each cites shows the requirement is not fully satisfied, which the status honestly records.</text>
</svg>